{"id":"u-a00a70c5-1ac1-4e30-a22b-351d5ebd6a33","src":"community","title":"Old School Bodybuilding Basic Training Level 1","author":"Tony T","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/7JW6Qo-old-school-bodybuilding-level-1","desc":"Level 1 basic training program Based on Arnold's Encyclopedia of Modern Bodybuilding\n\nStart with a full body warmup and stretching to prepare for workout.\n\nI do a light warmup set for each muscle group that I don't count as a working set. \n\nFor working sets pick a weight you can only do 8-10 reps of,  and do 3 sets of that weight with a 1 minute rest between sets. As you progress and get up to 12 reps increase the weight by 5-10% so you can only do 8 reps per set. This is double progression training, you adjust weight and reps to continuously challenge yourself as you get stronger. The 8-12 rep range is pretty standard for hypertrophy training.\nThere are a few possible variations, and some power training options. Full program with variations and power training options shown below. \n\n3 Day Split.     \nWorkout #1/ Workout #2 / Workout #3\n                            /                              /\nChest.             / Shoulders.   / Thighs\nBack                / Upper Arms / Calves\n                            / Forearms     / Lower Back \n\nAbdominals every workout day \n\nWORKOUT # 1\n________________________________________\nCHEST\n- Bench Press \n- Incline Press\n- Pullovers\n\nBACK\n- Lat Pulldowns (variation - chin ups to failure 4 sets)\n- Bent Over BB Row (Variation 1- Cable Low Row, Variation 2 - Bent over DB Row), Variation 3 - T-Bar row \n- Power training - Deadlifts, 3 sets of ten, 6, 4 to failure\n\nAbdominals \n- Crunches, 5 sets of 25\n\n_______________________________________WORKOUT # 2\n\nShoulders \n-Barbell Clean and Press \n-Dumb Bell Lateral Raises\n-Power Training, Heavy upright Rows 3 sets of 10, 6, 4 to failure\n\nUpper Arms\n-Standing Barbell Curls \n-Seated Dumbbell Curls\n-Close-Grip Press \n-Standing Barbell Triceps Extensions\n\nForearms \n-Wrist Curls\n-Reverse Wrist Curls\n\nAbdominals \n-Reverse Crunches,5 sets of 25\n________________________________________\nWORKOUT #3\n\nThighs \n-Squats\n-Lunges\n-Leg Curls \n\nCalves \n- Standing Calf Raises ( or on 45 degree Leg Press Machine) 5 sets of 25\n\nLower Back \n-Power Training \n - Straight Leg Deadlifts, 3 sets of 10, 6, 4 reps to failure \n - Good Mornings, 3 sets of 10, 6, 4 to failure\n\n(These low back movements also involve the Traps, Glutes, and Hamstrings, and help develop overall strength.)\n\nAbdominals \n- Crunches, 5 sets of 25 \n________________________________________\nStretches and Cool Down","level":["Beginner"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":90,"joins":3,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-09T02:55:23.950Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pullover (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bent Over Row (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}],"note":"Or swap for bent over Dumbbell Row"},{"n":"T-Bar Row","sets":[{"r":10,"x":5}],"note":"Variation instead of Bent over Row"},{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}],"note":"For power training option, 3 sets of 10, 6, 4 to failure"},{"n":"Abs Crunch (Weighted)","sets":[{"r":25,"x":5}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Clean and Press","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Upright Row (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}],"note":"For power training option, 3 sets of 10, 6, 4 to failure"},{"n":"Push Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Dumbbell Curl","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bench Press (Close Grip)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Tricep Extension (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Wrist Cu